From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Walks out past the top go out of the camera's sight; a tile
 in from the wall after a turn (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Roark leaving Oreburgh Mine's B2F walks east to a crate, a step north
round it, 2 east to the mine's wall, then north along it out of the wider
picture. He was taken away 9 rows above the middle, his feet still on
the taller screen. A way round past the top or bottom now goes on until
the walker is out of the camera's sight there (its feet and shadow above
the taller field's top, its head below its bottom), when there's a way
that far; else as far as before.

The turn a tile sooner along a wall (the way round ending outwards, then
up or down beside it) now also applies after earlier turns: Roark goes a
step east past the crate and up the middle of the passage.

---
diff --git a/src/scrcmd.c b/src/scrcmd.c
index d2f6aa71..5906b89d 100644
--- a/src/scrcmd.c
+++ b/src/scrcmd.c
@@ -2096,6 +2096,7 @@ extern int NitroPort_PixelField(void);
 #define PORT_WIDE_SENT_TILES    9  // a walk out ending here or further: off the DS's picture
 #define PORT_WIDE_TOP_TILES     9  // above the middle, beyond the top of the picture
 #define PORT_WIDE_BOTTOM_TILES  8  // below it, beyond the bottom
+#define PORT_WIDE_TALL_ROWS     24 // the taller field's rows past the DS's top and bottom (PORT_TALL_ROWS)
 #define PORT_WIDE_SCRIPTED_MAX  8
 #define PORT_WIDE_PATH_MAX      48 // steps of a way round
 #define PORT_WIDE_SEARCH_MAX    512
@@ -2364,6 +2365,7 @@ typedef struct PortWidePathSearch {
     u8 path[PORT_WIDE_PATH_MAX];
     u16 seen[PORT_WIDE_SEARCH_MAX];
     int seenCount;
+    BOOL outOfSight; // (ScrCmd_PortWidePastEdge: past the top or bottom as the camera has it too)
 } PortWidePathSearch;
 
